Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-16810) Improve kafka-consumer-perf-test to
 benchmark single partition
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Harsh Panchal created KAFKA-16810:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: Improve kafka-consumer-perf-test to benchmark single partition
                 Key: KAFKA-16810
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16810
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: New Feature
          Components: tools
            Reporter: Harsh Panchal


kafka-consumer-perf-test is a great tool to quickly check raw consumer performance. Currently, It subscribes to all the partitions and gives overall cluster performance, however If we want to test performance of single broker/partition, existing tool does not support.

We can introduce two optional flags --partitions and --offsets which gives flexibility to benchmark only specific partitions optionally from specified offsets.



