Hi


I would like to propose a change in the kafka-stream summary log=E3=80=82

Now the summary of stream-tread is record every two minutes, and not
support close  or update intervals.

When the kafka  is running=EF=BC=8C this is absolutely unnecessary and even=
 harmful
since it fills the logs and thus storage space with unwanted and useless
data.

I propose adding a configuration to control the output interval or disable
it

KIP=EF=BC=9A
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1049%3A+Add+config+lo=
g.summary.interval.ms+to+Kafka+Streams

