Hi, Artem,

Sorry for the late reply.

41. In the section "2PC transaction case with two epoch overflows", some of
the PrevProducerId are still set to -1.

45. Now that KIP-1022 is accepted, could we add a section on upgrade using
the transaction.version feature?

Thanks,

Jun

On Wed, Mar 20, 2024 at 10:25=E2=80=AFPM Artem Livshits
<alivshits@confluent.io.invalid> wrote:

> Hi Jun,
>
> Thank you for the comments.
>
> > 40. InitProducerId API: InitProducerId is an RPC,
>
> Updated.
>
> > 41. KIP-890 has changed slightly to always set PrevProducerId in the
> prepareCommit state
>
> Updated.
>
> > 42. In the following example, we overflow the ProducerId when
> ProducerEpoch reaches MAX-1.
>
> That's because there is an extra epoch bump that happens during the
> PrepareCommit state -- we need to increment the epoch to MAX so that we c=
an
> write markers with epoch+1.  I added a note after the example in the KIP.
>
> > 43. completeTransaction() is implemented in the client.
>
> Even if we had an explicit prepareTxn RPC, the client still must implemen=
t
> the protocol requirement to flush the data partitions before it calls
> prepareTxn RPC, which is pretty much most of the complexity of prepare.
>
> > 44.
>
> kafka.coordinator.transaction:type=3DTransactionStateManager,name=3DActiv=
eTransactionOpenTimeMax:
>
> Updated to
>
> *kafka.coordinator.transaction:type=3DTransactionStateManager,name=3DActi=
veTransactionOpenTimeMaxMs.*
>
> -Artem
>
> On Wed, Mar 13, 2024 at 2:04=E2=80=AFPM Jun Rao <jun@confluent.io.invalid=
> wrote:
>
> > Hi, Artem,
> >
> > Thanks for the explanation. Just a few more comments.
> >
> > 40. InitProducerId API: InitProducerId is an RPC, not an API. We
> typically
> > use API to refer to the public interfaces in the client libraries.
> >
> > 41. KIP-890 has changed slightly to always set PrevProducerId in the
> > prepareCommit state. So we need to change the examples in this KIP
> > accordingly. Also, the statement "Note that with vanilla KIP-890
> > transactions there are no cases when both NextProducerId and
> PrevProducerId
> > are set" is no longer true.
> >
> > 42. In the following example, we overflow the ProducerId when
> ProducerEpoch
> > reaches MAX-1.
> >     InitProducerId(true); TC STATE: Ongoing, ProducerId=3D42,
> > ProducerEpoch=3DMAX-1, PrevProducerId=3D-1, NextProducerId=3D73,
> > NextProducerEpoch=3D0; RESPONSE ProducerId=3D73, Epoch=3D0,
> > OngoingTxnProducerId=3D42, OngoingTxnEpoch=3DMAX-1
> > However, in the next example, we don't overflow the ProducerId when
> > ProducerEpoch reaches MAX-1.
> >     InitProducerId(true); TC STATE: Ongoing, ProducerId=3D42,
> > ProducerEpoch=3DMAX-1, PrevProducerId=3D-1, NextProducerId=3D73,
> > NextProducerEpoch=3DMAX; RESPONSE ProducerId=3D73, Epoch=3DMAX,
> > OngoingTxnProducerId=3D42, OngoingTxnEpoch=3DMAX-1
> > Should we be consistent?
> >
> > 43. completeTransaction() is implemented in the client. This may be ok.
> > However, it puts the burden on every client to implement it correctly. =
An
> > alternative is to do this on the server side through an RPC.
> >
> > 44.
> >
> >
> kafka.coordinator.transaction:type=3DTransactionStateManager,name=3DActiv=
eTransactionOpenTimeMax:
> > We typically add the time unit in the metric name.
> >
> > Jun
> >
> >
> > On Wed, Mar 6, 2024 at 2:49=E2=80=AFPM Artem Livshits
> > <alivshits@confluent.io.invalid> wrote:
> >
> > > Hi Jun,
> > >
> > > > So, for an application to switch from the 2PC option to the non-2PC
> > > option, is it just a config change or does the application code need =
to
> > be
